course: dictionary
lesson: 1662
title: Chloramine and the pool smell
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words are science words, and their meaning often hides in the clues around them. «Stinging eyes and the strong pool smell come mostly from chloramines, made when chlorine mixes with sweat and wee.» The sentence tells you that chloramines are made by mixing things together, and that they cause the stinging and the smell.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. «Red, stinging pool eyes are often caused by chloramines, made when chlorine mixes with sweat and wee in the water.» The words "caused by" show that chloramines are the reason for the red, stinging eyes, not the eyes themselves.
explain: The same word can describe a helpful chemical and an unpleasant smell. Some water companies add chloramine to tap water to kill germs and keep it safe to drink. At the swimming pool, chloramines are the smelly chemicals that form when chlorine mixes with sweat and wee.
fact: Chloramine is a chemical made from chlorine and ammonia.
fact: Some water companies use chloramine to kill germs in tap water.
fact: At swimming pools, chloramines form when chlorine mixes with sweat and wee.
fact: Chloramines cause the «pool smell» and red, sore eyes.
fact: Never mix bleach and ammonia cleaners: they make chloramine gas, which is harmful to breathe.
exercise: «Stinging eyes and the strong pool smell come mostly from chloramines.» What causes the pool smell? | *Chloramines | Clean water from the tap | Swimming hats | Sunshine on the water
exercise: What mixes together to make chloramines in a pool? | Mud and leaves | Sand and sunshine | *Chlorine mixing with sweat and wee | Soap and cold water
exercise: Why do some water companies use chloramine? | To make the water taste sweet | To make tap water smell of the pool | To colour the water blue | *To kill germs and keep tap water safe
test: What should you do before you swim to reduce chloramines? | Swim as fast as you can | *Shower and use the toilet first | Hold your breath underwater | Put on extra sun cream only
test: Why is it dangerous to mix bleach and ammonia cleaners? | It makes the bottle heavier | *It makes chloramine gas, which is harmful to breathe | It makes the cleaner taste nicer | It makes a bright light
exam: What is chloramine made from? | Sweat and salt | Sugar and water | *Chlorine and ammonia | Bleach and water
